    },
    "Your device encrypts your profile, Kits and conversations before upload. The server receives ciphertext, opaque IDs and storage metadata, never your content key." : {

    },
    "Your first entry starts here." : {

    },
    "Your messages, requested Kit definitions and synthetic test results are shared with the selected inference provider only after approval. When you ask to use connected GitHub tools, their sanitized read-only profile and public repository results are also shared with the conversation’s provider and saved in encrypted conversation history. Connecting or checking GitHub alone does not share account data with the provider. Saved Kit entries, vault keys and connection credentials are never included by tools. Personal information you type in a message is still disclosed." : {

